Wave 3 is running again after the first attempt stopped on your plan's session limit (it reset at 7:10).

The first attempt ran about 20 minutes, and none of its work was lost. Each package had uncommitted work in its worktree, about 25,000 lines across the seven packages. I committed it as work-in-progress on each package's branch and cleared the worktrees. The new builders continue from those branches: they review that work critically (it never passed `pnpm check`), finish it, and squash the work-in-progress commits away.

Wave 3 runs seven packages in parallel, so it could hit the session limit again. If it does, I'll save the progress the same way and resume after the reset.

When it lands I'll report:
- the tools judge: convex, playwright and GitHub through Executor from a deployed thread;
- the Claude `kill -9` judges;
- paste and attachments;
- the transcript.
